     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Status of Implementation Progress: 1) - 5MW Uliastai solar PV: Technical commission was done in Oct 2022 and state commission was done in Nov 2022. The plant started to supply electricity to the soum grid from 26 Nov 2022. - Altai soum hybrid system: Technical and state commissioning was completed in Jul 2022. The plant started to supply electricity to the soum grid from 28 Jun 2022. The hybrid energy system was inaugurated in Aug 2022. - 10MW Altai solar PV: The plant started to supply electricity to the soum grid from Sep 2023. - 10MW Umunogovi wind and 5MW Telmen wind: Feasibility study for a combined subproject is being finalized. Bidding is targeted in Q4 2023. - 10MW Moron solar PV: Works are ongoing and expected to be completed by Oct 2023. 2) - SGHP Batch 1 (Khovd): The system was commissioned and turned over in Sep 2021, and accepted in Jan 2022. - SGHP Batch 2 (Uliastai and Bayankhongor): Uliastai was completed and commissioned in Apr 2023. Bayankhongor SGHP works are ongoing. - SGHP Batch 3 (Ulaangom and Altai): Works are ongoing.3) Contract for training of AUES staff for solar and battery storage systems has been signed by MOE on 21 Mar 2023 and submitted to ADB in Apr/May 2023. Training to be completed by Nov 2023.The consultant has submitted first draft of investment plan to PMU on 16 Jun 2020. Electricity and heat demand forecasts were prepared, and least cost supply expansions modelled in 2021/2022. Investment planning activities can resume with the Investment Plan/Renewable Energy Policy completed by end of May 2023.</narrative>
